# Performance and Optimization Standards

## Response Time Targets
- Interface discovery: < 100ms
- Table formatting: < 50ms
- Overall CLI response: < 200ms
- Vendor lookup (cached): < 10ms
- Vendor lookup (uncached): < 500ms

## Memory Usage Guidelines
- Keep memory usage under 10MB for typical interface counts
- Use efficient data structures (lists over dicts where appropriate)
- Avoid loading large datasets into memory unnecessarily
- Implement lazy loading for vendor databases
- Monitor memory usage during development

## Caching Strategy
- Cache vendor lookup results persistently
- Cache system interface information during single execution
- Use appropriate cache expiration for dynamic data
- Implement cache size limits to prevent memory bloat
- Consider cache warming for frequently accessed data

## System Call Optimization
- Minimize system calls during interface discovery
- Batch operations where possible
- Use efficient file reading for system information
- Avoid repeated calls to the same system resources
- Cache system call results when safe to do so

## Data Structure Efficiency
- Use appropriate data types for network addresses
- Minimize object creation in tight loops
- Use generators for large datasets
- Avoid unnecessary string operations
- Profile code to identify bottlenecks

## Future Performance Considerations
- Design for real-time monitoring scenarios
- Consider event-driven architecture for updates
- Plan for handling hundreds of interfaces
- Optimize for both CPU and I/O bound operations
- Keep performance in mind for cross-platform compatibility

## Performance Testing
- Include performance benchmarks in test suite
- Test with realistic interface counts
- Monitor memory usage during tests
- Profile code execution for bottlenecks
- Set performance regression tests
